-- Test Description
-- This test ensures the proper use of pause frames by the GEM in both transmission and reception.
--
-- Functional Coverage
-- � Check the pause frame is able to be recognised by the GEM, then check the
--   system counts down and issues all relevant interrupts.
-- � Check all four valid addresses, only register 1 hit shall cause valid
--   RX received OK and associated interrupt, plus DMA activity.
-- � Check that when pause is disabled the frame is treated as a normal 
--   data frame.
-- � Check that when pause disabled it correctly handles frame destination 
--   address.
-- � Re-enable pause and check that a new incoming pause value overwrites
--   an existing one.
-- � Overwrite an existing pause time with a zero pause time. 
-- � Receive a non-zero pause time with wrong OPCODE. (should be ignored)
-- � Receive a non-zero pause time with wrong TYPE-ID and proper pause frame destination address.
-- � Receive a non-zero pause time with wrong TYPE-ID and local 1 
--   destination address. (should be copied to memory)
-- � Receive a non-zero pause time with everything right except pause frame 
--   destination address. (should be ignored)
-- � Receive a non-zero pause time with everything right but give it
--   a CRC error (should be set pause timer)
-- � Test the interrupt mask for bit 13 of interrupt status (pause zero)
-- � Test the interrupt mask for bit 12 of interrupt status (pause received)
-- � Check full range pause count (0xffff)
-- � Test that pause frames are not copied when the do not copy pause frames bit
--   is set in the network configuration register.
--
-- Detailed test description
-- Note:  The retry test pin is set in the network configuration register to change the decrementer time from 512 bit period to 1 bit period to make the test quicker.
--
-- Pause time frame structure: 
-- Destination address	Source address	Type (GEM control frame)	Pause opcode 	Pause time
-- 0x0180C2000001	6 bytes	0x8808	0x0001	2 bytes
-- 
-- 1. Initialise the GEM for 10 mode operation.
-- 2. Set pause enable in the network configuration register
-- 3. Check reset state of loopback, half_duplex and extint pins.
-- 4. Check reset state of registers.
-- 5. Enable receive buffer and all interrupts.
-- 6. Set pause enable bit in the network configuration register
-- 7. Reset retry test pin in the network configuration register.
-- 8. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches register 1,
--    type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x0005.  
--    (Frame should be copied to memory)
-- 9. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause frame address 
--    0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, Pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time 
--    to be set is 0x00FF. (Frame should not be copied to memory)
-- 10. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches register 1, 
--     type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x00FF. 
--     (Pause frames should be treated as a normal data frame.  In this particular 
--     case the pause frame should be written to memory since the destination address 
--     matches the address in specific address register one.)
-- 11. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause frame 
--     address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and 
--     pause time to be set is 0x0055. (Since the destination address matches the 
--     pause frame address, the frame should not be written to memory)
-- 12. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause frame 
--     address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and 
--     pause time to be set is 0x00AA.  However, shortly afterwards, receive a 
--     pause frame with the length counter equal to zero.  
--     (This should disable the pause functionality immediately)
-- 13. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause frame 
--     address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0002  and 
--     pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  (The wrong opcode value is received. 
--     Therefore, the pause frame should be ignored)
-- 14. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause 
--     frame address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8807, pause op-code = 0x0001 
--     and pause time to be set is 0x00FF. (The wrong type-id value is received. 
--     Therefore, the pause frame should be ignored)
-- 15. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches register 1, 
--     type field = 0x8807, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x0005.  
--     (The wrong type-id value was received but the destination address matched the 
--     local address.  Therefore, the frame should be written to memory)
-- 16. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause frame address
--     0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and
--     pause time to be set is 0x00FF. (The wrong destination address value was received.
--     Therefore, the frame should not be written to memory)
-- 17. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause frame 
--     address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and 
--     pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  However, there is a crc error.  
--     (The pause frame should be ignored)
-- 18. Disable pause received interrupt (bit 12).
-- 19. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause frame 
--     address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and 
--     pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  (There should be no pause frame received 
--     interrupt set in the interrupt status register)
-- 20. Enable pause received interrupt (bit 12).
-- 21. Disable pause time zero interrupt (bit 13).
-- 22. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause 
--     frame address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 
--     and pause time to be set is 0x00FF.  (There should be no pause time zero 
--     interrupt set in the interrupt status register)
-- 23. Enable pause zero interrupt (bit 13).
-- 24. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches pause 
--     frame address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 
--     and pause time to be set is 0x0FFF. 
-- 25. Disable pause enable interrupt and retry test bit. 
-- 26. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches register 1, 
--     type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x00FF. 
--     (Pause frames should be treated as a normal data frame.  In this particular 
--     case the pause frame should be written to memory since the destination address 
--     matches the address in specific address register one. Also, the pause counter
--     should not be set since the enable pause frame bit is reset.)
-- 27. Enable the pause time bit, copy all frames bit, do not copy pause
--     frames bit, external address match enable bit and pause enable bit.
-- 28. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches register 1,
--     type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and pause time to be set is 0x0005.  
--     Try matching on specific address, a broadcast frame, a hash match, a type match 
--     and external match. However, the frame should not be copied to memory because 
--     bit (23) the do not copy puase frame bit is set)
-- 29. Check the status and statistics registers and ensure that the above operations 
--     were handled properly
-- 30. Receive a pause frame where the destination address matches the pause frame 
--     address 0x0180C2000001, type field = 0x8808, pause op-code = 0x0001 and 
--     pause time to be set is 0x0020.  Once the pause timer is about to decrement to
--     zero, receive a zero length pause frame (tests the hanshaking logic).  
--     This should cause only one pause time zero interrupt to be received.
